{"id":177269535646084,"type":"album","name":"Minute by Minute","artist":"The Doobie Brothers","year":1978,"weight":13,"info":{"cover":"https://ia601808.us.archive.org/11/items/mbid-da7c841b-8494-47b9-94b2-66dcc4a6e5f8/mbid-da7c841b-8494-47b9-94b2-66dcc4a6e5f8-16491795590.jpg","yt":"V_Eriq_jNZY","links":{"rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/the-doobie-brothers/minute-by-minute"},"desc":"Minute by Minute is the eighth studio album by American rock band The Doobie Brothers, released in 1978. The album contains their biggest hit, the Grammy-winning \"What a Fool Believes,\" which was co-written by Kenny Loggins and simultaneously released on his 1978 album Nightwatch. \"Depending on You\" and the title track were also released as singles. The album would be the last to include members Jeff \"Skunk\" Baxter and John Hartman. It is the most-honored Doobie's album, being awarded four Grammys at the 22nd Grammy Awards - more than any other album by the band. ."},"artist_ref":{"id":65810346942356,"name":"The Doobie Brothers","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Doobie_brothers.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":18872195504512,"type":"genre","name":"Pop Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":740,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":251671925246370,"type":"genre","name":"Soft Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":418,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":186201380116213,"type":"genre","name":"classic rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":268,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":25930810330885,"type":"genre","name":"AOR","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":234,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":136113600818764,"type":"genre","name":"Yacht Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":215,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"}],"lists":[{"id":254136942605146,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Yacht Rock","src":"musthear","grp":"rateyourmusic","list_year":null,"rank":33,"year":null,"note":null,"total":200,"scaruffi":null},{"id":82958032046503